---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Refund Policy & 30-Minute Guarantee | CQ Buddy" description="Three layers of protection: the 30-minute guarantee, free cancellation 48+ hours ahead, and a deposit rule that respects both sides.">
  <section>
    <div class="container" style="max-width:760px;">
      <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1>Refunds &amp; the 30-minute guarantee</h1>
      <p class="muted small">Last updated: 4 November 2026 · v1.0</p>
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>1. The 30-minute guarantee</h2>
        <p>Any in-person service (First Night, Private Day, Food Walk): if within the first 30 minutes you tell us this isn't for you, we refund <strong>everything you've paid, including the deposit</strong>, and help you continue on your own. No forms, no debate.</p>
        <h2>2. Cancellation before the service</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>48+ hours before:</strong> full refund of the deposit, any reason.</li>
          <li><strong>Inside 48 hours:</strong> we keep the deposit if we can't re-book the host's day — but if we fill the slot, you get it back.</li>
          <li><strong>No-show without notice:</strong> deposit retained; the balance is never charged.</li>
        </ul>
        <h2>3. Concierge windows</h2>
        <p>Concierge is refundable in full before the 24-hour window starts. Once started, unused hours don't roll over or refund — but if we badly miss our 30-minute response promise, we extend the window for free, and that part's on us.</p>
        <h2>4. How refunds are paid</h2>
        <p>Same channel you paid through, within 7 days of the decision. If you paid cash in China, we return it via Alipay or WeChat transfer.</p>
        <h2>5. The spirit of this page</h2>
        <p>We're a new company asking strangers to trust us with their first night in a strange city. Fair refund terms are how we earn that trust before reviews exist. If a situation doesn't fit the rules above, message us — a founder decides edge cases, and leans toward the guest.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
